 ## Background
-3-D SPIHT was introduced by B.-J. Kim, Z. Xiong, and W. A. Pearlman in "Low bit-rate scalable video coding with 3-D set partitioning in hierarchical trees (3-D SPIHT)" (IEEE Trans. Circuits Syst. Video Technol., vol. 10, pp. 1365–1374, Dec. 2000) [S1]. It extends the 2-D SPIHT algorithm [5] to 3-D data by treating wavelet coefficients as 3-D spatio-temporal orientation trees [S1]. It is widely used in medical image compression, particularly for volumetric data like CT and MR scans [S1].
+3-D SPIHT was introduced by B.-J. Kim, Z. Xiong, and W. A. Pearlman in "Low bit-rate scalable video coding with 3-D set partitioning in hierarchical trees (3-D SPIHT)" (IEEE Trans. Circuits Syst. Video Technol., vol. 10, pp. 1365–1374, Dec. 2000) [S1]. It extends the 2-D SPIHT algorithm to 3-D data by treating wavelet coefficients as 3-D spatio-temporal orientation trees [S1]. It is widely used in medical image compression, particularly for volumetric data like CT and MR scans [S1].
 
